.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-3.0-or-later
.TH PKGINFO 8 "" "imai #VERSION#" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
pkginfo \- display CRUX package information
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pkginfo
.RI [ \-r " root" ] " mode"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pkginfo
queries the installed package database or a package archive without modifying
packages. Specify exactly one query mode; repeated mode options are errors.
.SH QUERY MODES
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-installed
List installed package names and versions in package-name order.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-list " " package|file
List the inventory of an installed package or members of an existing package
archive. An installed package name takes precedence over a filesystem pathname
of the same spelling. If no package name matches, an existing pathname selects
archive inspection. This mode opens the installed database even for an archive;
unlike footprint mode, it therefore requires an accessible database.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-owner " " pattern
List owners of installed files matching a POSIX extended regular expression.
Matching uses inventory names prefixed with /; displayed file names retain
their stored spelling. No match prints a message and returns zero.
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-footprint " " file
Print the archive footprint, including file types, permissions, ownership,
names and link or device information. This output is consumed by
.BR pkgmk (8).
No installed database is required for this mode.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-root " " path
Select the package database under another system's root instead of /.
Archive arguments are still interpreted in the caller's filesystem.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the invoked command name, imai identity and version, then exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help and exit.
.SH ARCHIVE VALIDATION
Supported package compression formats are gzip, bzip2, xz, lzip and zstd.
The complete compression stream and tar payload are consumed before query
output is printed. Damaged input fails without partial archive-query output,
a deliberate difference from legacy header-error handling.
Decoded temporary streams require disk space; checksums detect some corruption
but do not authenticate packages. Checksums cannot detect all alterations in
formats that omit them.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero indicates successful completion, including an owner query with no matches.
Invalid arguments, invalid regular expressions, database or archive errors,
and output errors return nonzero.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/pkg/db
Plain-text package database; queries hold a shared directory lock.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pkgadd (8),
.BR pkgrm (8),
.BR pkgmk (8),
.BR rejmerge (8)
